e  your work up your treatment and so on so  forth this is where it's probably really  important to mention that during med  school I started an Instagram account  and initially it was dr. Mikey or  something it was like dr underscore mike  with like three e's or something like  that  because i wanted to show what it was  like to be just an ordinary medical  student nothing special but be able to  enjoy your life be able to have a  balance between exercise education  social life going out enjoying nice  events but still doing well in school  because i feel there exists a stigma and  i really think it's a stigma that if you  go into medical school you have to give  up your life myth busted that is  complete BS everybody needs to study  very hard in medical school but it  doesn't mean that you have to give up  your life you could study hard you can  study smart and you could do very well  while still enjoying your life so what i  was doing i was sort of doing a what was  popular back then a lot of those at  myspace it came after myspace but it was  one of those it was like not a blog it  was xanga basically what I was doing was  showing my life through the internet I  was living my life through the internet  and I was blocking this was a new thing  that people were doing in the mid to  early 2000s xanga live journal these  were popular blogging sites but I was  like I want to do that on Instagram I  want to do a photo blog of my life so I  took selfies of me in the operating room  I took selfies with my dog I took  selfies with my dad at fancy events and  throughout New York City and people  really enjoyed what I was doing  so I build up a pretty significant  following for the average person  somewhere twenty thirty thousand  followers going into residency it was a  running joke during my intern year that  people that knew me well they would make  jokes like oh dr. mike has a lot of  followers on Instagram with his twenty  thousand he was a celebrity  and look we had 