d of that residency year so I  did my first week of vacation in August  September of my second year and guess  what I'm on vacation  I'm in Florida and all of a sudden one  of my buddies texted me  and he said hey man you're on BuzzFeed  and I'm like oh man that's really cool  because while I've done some little news  articles here and there I've done some  scientific publications I've never had  something as big as BuzzFeed mention me  and I was like oh that's cool I read the  story it wasn't anything about my  medical accomplishments it was hot  doctor and husky and I was like oh  that's nice like awesome compliment  pretty exciting I didn't think anything  would come from it and then as the day  went on I started getting more and more  texts from people not only about  BuzzFeed now now elite daily then  Huffington Post and then AOL calm then  time then Cosmo then glamour and all of  a sudden my inbox starts imploding I  mean everybody's emailing me that week  Ellen DeGeneres people Steve Harvey  people everybody is saying if you do our  show you can do our show but you can't  do their show you if you come on Fox you  can't do CBS by the way I don't remember  exactly who said what but this was all  being said and I'm a resident I know  nothing about media I have no  representation I have no guides I don't  even know anyone in the industry really  I always faced with a choice because I'm  a professional and I'm going into a  professional field and I had to decide  do you embrace this hot topic sorry this  hot doctor topic as something that you  want to go in front of millions of  people on television and talk about as  if it's something you truly care about I  didn't really care that people are  calling me hot doctor but what I did  care was that suddenly millions of  people were interested to listen to me  and I viewed that as an opportunity  honestly was insane  I gained 750,000 followers in those two  weeks my phone was just I had to turn  off notifications for 